parameters.text:
=Job title: {{ $json.job_title }}
Job description: {{ $json.job_description }}
Experience level: {{ $json.experience_level }}
Interview language: {{ $json.language }}
Number of questions: {{ $json.num_questions }}

Generate exactly {{ $json.num_questions }} interview questions for this job:
- The first question must be a self-introduction question.
- Include a mix of Technical, Behavioral, and Problem-Solving questions relevant to the job.

Rules:
- Write natural, grammatically correct questions in {{ $json.language }}.
- Match the difficulty to this experience level: {{ $json.experience_level }}.
- Do not assume specific technologies unless they appear in the job description.
- Keep each question short enough to be asked out loud in a spoken interview.

Return ONLY a valid JSON array, no extra text, no markdown:
[{"id": 1, "question": "...", "type": "Self-Introduction"}, {"id": 2, "question": "...", "type": "Technical"}]

parameters.jsCode:
const item = $input.first().json;
const raw = item.text || item.output || '';

// ننضّف أي markdown أو نص زيادة حوالين الـ JSON
let clean = String(raw).replace(/```json|```/g, '').trim();
const start = clean.indexOf('[');
const end = clean.lastIndexOf(']');
if (start !== -1 && end !== -1) {
  clean = clean.slice(start, end + 1);
}

let questions = [];
try {
  questions = JSON.parse(clean);
} catch (e) {
  return [{ json: { text: raw, questions: [], parse_error: true, error_message: e.message } }];
}

const text = questions
  .map(q => `${q.id}. ${q.question}`)
  .join('\n');

return [{ json: { text, questions, parse_error: false } }];

